  "source_decisions": {
    "as": "The Bālamanoramā on 3.1.66 explicitly gives -āmāse in both 3sg and 1sg. It restricts the h of 7.4.52 to sārvadhātuka in this analysis. The comparison archive has 1sg -āmāhe for each curādi stem.",
    "bhu": "Selected a-vowel copy follows the Kāśikā/Nyāsa at 7.4.73 and the Siddhāntakaumudī example at 3.1.66. The Prakriyāsarvasva at 3.4.81 explicitly gives both 2pl dental and retroflex, and separately reports a u-copy interpretation of bhāva/karman (bubhūve). No alternate series has been inferred into this grid from that report.",
    "orthography": "At a word boundary before c and b both anusvāra and the corresponding homorganic nasal are retained under 8.4.59. They represent one auxiliary choice each."
  }
